 {"version_id": "prompt-10", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Failure triage and bounded iteration", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient validation and iterative debugging", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, first perform repository reconnaissance: locate the primary implementation, all callers, related subclasses or alternate backends, existing regression tests, and analogous behavior elsewhere in the repository.", "replace": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, validate in layers: syntax/import checks, the smallest relevant unit test, neighboring tests for the same component, then the broader affected suite. After every failure, classify it as an implementation failure, test/setup failure, unrelated environmental failure, or newly exposed regression; gather the relevant traceback and source evidenc"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.87, "reasoning_soundness": 0.84, "execution_accuracy": 0.88, "output_integrity": 0.89}, "aggregate": 0.87, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.97}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.97}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.34}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.32}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 0x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.035, "why": "Layered testing with explicit failure classification most directly improves iterative debugging and limits wasted edits, making it the strongest execution-oriented candidate. It does not substantially improve initial diagnosis or edge-case design, and bounded iteration can still stop before broader regressions are found."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-11", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Compatibility matrix with explicit omission semantics", "target_failure_mode": "Edge-case and regression handling", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, first perform repository reconnaissance: locate the primary implementation, all callers, related subclasses or alternate backends, existing regression tests, and analogous behavior elsewhere in the repository.", "replace": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, define a compatibility matrix covering the documented case, empty and null values, missing versus explicitly supplied defaults, malformed and partially specified inputs, exact boundaries, zero and negative values, repeated calls, and relevant subclasses or alternate backends. For each case, record the current behavior, required behavior, exc"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.88, "reasoning_soundness": 0.81, "execution_accuracy": 0.8, "output_integrity": 0.9}, "aggregate": 0.8475, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.33}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.3}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 0x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0125, "why": "The matrix covers omission, null, malformed, boundary, and repeated-call behavior that commonly causes framework and scientific-library regressions, improving output integrity on difficult cases. However, its breadth can encourage speculative handling and overfitting without first establishing repository-specific semantics, so reasoning and execution fall below the stronger validation candidates."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-12", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Metamorphic and negative-case regression checks", "target_failure_mode": "Edge-case and regression handling", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "django__django-16938", "astropy__astropy-13033"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "trae_agent/agent/trae_agent.py", "find": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, first perform repository reconnaissance: locate the primary implementation, all callers, related subclasses or alternate backends, existing regression tests, and analogous behavior elsewhere in the repository.", "replace": "Before editing a framework or scientific-library change, identify the behavior-preserving relations that should remain true, such as equivalent representations producing equivalent results, repeated operations remaining stable, and unrelated parameters not changing the result. Test the requested case plus negative cases, boundary transitions, invalid inputs, and nearby legacy cases. Pay special at"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.86, "reasoning_soundness": 0.83, "execution_accuracy": 0.82, "output_integrity": 0.88}, "aggregate": 0.8475, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-15100", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "pytest-dev__pytest-7432", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16938", "score": 0.32}, {"instance_id": "astropy__astropy-13033", "score": 0.31}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "proposed_not_applied", "apply_note": "find-block matched 0x (need exactly 1)", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0125, "why": "Metamorphic and negative checks help expose regressions that ordinary examples miss, particularly around repeated operations and unrelated parameters. The approach is less directly actionable than a focused reproduction or layered triage and risks assuming invalid behavior-preserving relations, keeping gains modest."}
