narrowest relevant test or a focused reproduction, inspect the complete failure output, and iterate on the implementation until the focused checks pass. Then run the broader relevant test groups and, before finalizing, perform an adversarial compatibility review covering public API signatures, exception types and messages, ordering, mutability, numerical precision, serialization, subclass behavior, and interactions with neighboring features; reject any change lacking evidence for intentional behavior differences.
